# Koh, the Face Stealer (CR 607.2a, 607.5): Koh's enters trigger exiles one of Bot2's Emperors of Bones on turn 3, and its dies
# trigger exiles the other, which Bot1's Lightning Bolt kills on turn 5. Bot1 pays 1 life to choose the first Emperor, and at the
# beginning of combat that card's lent trigger exiles the Llanowar Elves Bot2's Shock killed. In the second main phase Bot1 pays
# to choose the other Emperor, then pays again to choose the first one once more, and adapts with its lent "{1}{B}: Adapt 2".
# The first Emperor's abilities are lent to Koh anew: a fresh acquisition, linked only to one another and not to the ones Koh
# had of that same card before it chose the other (CR 607.5, "regardless of what other abilities the object ... may have had in
# the past"). So its lent "put a creature card exiled with this creature onto the battlefield" finds nothing, and the Elves the
# earlier lending exiled stays in exile.

